cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tseffects: Dynamic Effects from Single-Equation Time Series Models in Python"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the method paper and the original R package."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roudane
    given-names: Merwan
    email: merwanroudane920@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/merwanroudane/tsseffect"
url: "https://merwanroudane.github.io/tsseffect/"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
version: 0.5.1
date-released: "2026-10-28"
keywords:
  - time series
  - econometrics
  - autoregressive distributed lag
  - error correction model
  - impulse response function
  - long-run multiplier
  - interaction effects
  - delta method
abstract: >-
  Recovers dynamic inferences from autoregressive distributed lag (ADL) models
  and Generalized Error-Correction Models (GECM): impulse and step response
  functions, arbitrary shock histories, long-run multipliers, fitted
  trajectories, and the conditional effects implied by a multiplicative
  interaction. Every quantity is built as an algebraic formula in the model's
  coefficient names and then evaluated by the delta method, so one
  standard-error machinery covers them all. A Python port of the R package
  tseffects by Soren Jordan, Garrett N. Vande Kamp and Reshi Rajan.
